  {
    "label": "Support Graduate Student Education The funding for graduate education has become increasingly threatened, and the math department at UCLA faces many challenges in this regard. Graduate students are not only trained here; they are also often integral to the research itself. In applied mathematics, graduate students frequently work hand in hand with faculty on impactful projects. In pure mathematics, the mentorship model—faculty guiding students through their research—is a crucial, irreplaceable learning experience. Your philanthropic support is needed at this crucial time. Donate Now",
